{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/982111-proximus-legacies","id":982111,"title":"Proximus Legacies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-05T07:27:06-07:00","id":982111,"title":"Proximus Legacies","content":"Probably should have ended with a question mark, but it really isn't a question, since I know the answer is currently &quot;no&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm more interested in exploring if they <i>might</i> exist, and how would one go about it.<br /> <br /> So, Proximi have some access to Awakened magic, but lack the full power and awareness. Or Gnosis. Still, they have souls, and Legacies are basically just Soul Shaping according to Supernal principles, right? So, even if they need external help, would it be possible for a Proximus to pick up their own kind of Legacy? Maybe basing Arcana requirements off known Blessings, and Gnosis off of Willpower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:35:58-07:00","id":982194,"title":"","content":"In my game, I'd allow it, but the result would be a new mage with the minimum Gnosis to begin in the legacy. Metaphysically, that seems correct to me, and it certainly avoids some balance issues.<br /> Dunno how helpful that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T23:25:11-07:00","id":982568,"title":"","content":"I feel like being a Proximi is <i>already</i> essentially adding a Legacy to a Sleepwalker. If you want a Proximi to be more powerful just have them Awaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T06:57:48-07:00","id":982670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/982111-proximus-legacies?p=982568#post982568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like being a Proximi is <i>already</i> essentially adding a Legacy to a Sleepwalker. If you want a Proximi to be more powerful just have them Awaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. Legacy Attainments let you do things without fear of Paradox, Dissonance, and/or Dispelling. A Proximus having those options might make them useful in certain circumstances without having the full power and baggage of a full Mage.<br /> <br /> Just more options to potentially make Proximi more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:52:27-07:00","id":985087,"title":"","content":"So is this pointless rumination, or does anyone have any ideas regarding potential mechanics? Or would a Mystery Cult model that grants Supernatural Merits (modeled on Mage spells) work well enough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T19:17:33-07:00","id":985212,"title":"","content":"I have some thoughts:<ul><li>Proximi have to join a Legacy with a Ruling Arcanum from their family Arcana. They can't found their own Legacy, and they can't change Legacy later any more than a Mage can.</li> <li>Proximi can <i>only</i> learn the secrets of a Legacy from a teacher. They lack the knowledge and power to learn from a soul or a daimonomikon.</li> <li>Only the 1st and second Attainments. Proximi aren't Awakened, so their souls aren't malleable enough to take on more advanced Attainments. They can't choose Novel Attainments.</li> <li>They can't join by virtue of Order, or by Praxis. They need to either come from a family with the right Parent Path, or know a Blessing that matches one of the Legacy's Attainments. If they gain an Attainment version of one of their Blessings, they don't get a refund, sorry Charlie.</li> <li>They don't get an increase to their Mana Pool, nor do they get access to Paradox-free Reach for their Blessings, but they do get access to their Legacy's Oblations in addition to their families', and their Attainments get their built-in Reach and are Paradox-free like normal.</li> <li>Still no Yantras. Legacies can't help there.</li> <li>If the Proximus Awakens, they retain their Legacy, and the Attainments acquired under its auspices. They must place at least 1 Dot in each Ruling Arcanum, from their Path and their Legacy.</li> <li>Aside from Gnosis and Arcana, Proximi need to meet all prerequisites normally. If they Awaken, they retain their Legacy Attainments, but they may function erratically until they meet the all the requirements.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}